d any of our people  to the uk or germany for example to meet  airports without quarantine  for 20 for 14 days and despite that  ireland has  one of the highest and fastest writing  covert case rates in europe  now we think by the way that the focus  on covert case rates is completely  misplaced  uh because what's evident in the second  wave is that  rising covert case rates is not  translating into hospitals being  overwhelmed or icu's being flooded with  people  in ireland our hospitals and icus are  essentially empty  and yet we are pandering to this uh  covent case rate nonsense and  while at the same time the germans and  the italians have been allowing intra-eu  air travel since the first of july their  covet case rates are about half that of  the uk  and ireland of ireland uh the uk is  uh reasonably low as well and yet  we still have these bizarre restrictions  in the uk for example  they're locking down regions like bolton  and preston but then they say nobody can  travel to spain despite the fact that in  spain  while there are high covert case rates  in the main cities of barcelona and  madrid  there are no covent case rates in the  canaries the lyrics in the tourism  uh hot spots so there's no common sense  and the industry is calling for more  effective testing at airports that at  least  would help us to continue to deliver  safe air travel we've been you know  doing that since the first of july  ourselves  um and we're also calling on the  government to um you know  reduce apd the travel attacks on air  travel  if richie sunak who cleverly came up  with a  you know eat out to help out scheme uh  gave people 50 reductions on their meals  why haven't they reduced apd in the uk  which is still  a an unfair and egregious tax but  that stops people visiting the uk  michael i just want to pick up on what  you said about airport testing there  because of course boris johnson's ruled  it out on the grounds of airport tests  only pick up seven percent of cases